  "interpretation": {
    "pending_root_convention": "corpus fillResult root = suffix.back() = check_token[-1]; with the overlap splice prev_tokens = accept_tokens[i*D : i*D+accept_lens] that token is the pending token at position seq_lens, and row-0 logits are its greedy continuation.",
    "splice_is_load_bearing": "without the splice the draft root is the last already-cached token; the stale root changes the committed greedy output, so a stale/mis-spliced root is a correctness fault, not draft quality.",
    "accept_lens_includes_bonus": "accept_lens = num_correct_drafts + 1 must advance both seq_lens and the KV front; dropping the bonus desyncs the engine prefix from physical KV and diverges.",
    "limits": "perfect corpus + linear chain; no real trie, attention kernel, FlashInfer packing, CUDA graph, overlap scheduling or batch nondeterminism."
  }
